    {
      "evidence": "template/scripts/delegated_write_guard.py:1019-1024. `target` is only checked for None, then `Path(target)` is called with no type check. A non-string value raises an uncaught exception and the hook never emits a decision. This was already the case before the change and is outside the delta, but it is the same containment gap the change targets. A one-line isinstance(target, str) check that denies would close it, and the new deny test could cover it.",
      "id": "guard-non-string-target-crash-fails-open",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The change closes the fail-open for a missing target key, but the neighbouring non-string target case is unchanged. A payload like {\"file_path\": 123} or {\"file_path\": [..]} makes Path(target) raise TypeError, so the hook exits non-zero with a traceback instead of emitting a deny. Claude Code normally treats a non-2 hook failure as non-blocking, so the write may proceed."
    }
  ],
